visible meadow roots have zero stock on ordinary soil with moisture 0.65; my health is 100 and I own two roots. I do not know which propagation or tending methods work.\\\",\\\"inputs\\\":\\\"Existing depleted food plants, suitable ground, and any seeds, planting material, tools or water that a feasible method actually requires; required inputs are presently unknown.\\\",\\\"costs\\\":\\\"Unknown; specify realistic time, effort, materials and learning prerequisites. No free food or instant replenishment is assumed.\\\",\\\"effects\\\":\\\"Enable an actual trial of food cultivation or plant tending, with observable progress and conditional harvest rather than guaranteed yield. Preserve existing resource and growth constraints.\\\"}},\\\"repeat\\\":1,\\\"until\\\":null,\\\"guard\\\":null}],\\\"repeat\\\":1,\\\"until\\\":null,\\\"interrupts\\\":[],\\\"notes\\\":[\\\"The previous search left two owned roots; nearby visible roots and tubers are empty.\\\",\\\"Ivo reports personally eating berries safely, but I have not independently established their nutrition or toxicity.\\\",\\\"Search costs are bounded; rest restores energy, not food.\\\"],\\\"preferences\\\":[\\\"Keep an energy reserve and prioritize personally verified safe food.\\\",\\\"Prefer learning a sustainable food method over repeatedly exhausting the same patches.\\\"],\\\"projects\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"reliable-food\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"active\\\",\\\"question\\\":\\\"How can I maintain a dependable supply of safe food locally?\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":[\\\"Root nutrition is recorded as 14 and toxicity zero.\\\",\\\"At tick 81 I own two roots and 0.9 berry; health is 100, satiety 91.1 and energy approximately 39.99.\\\",\\\"Visible meadow roots and marsh tuber plants have zero stock at tick 81.\\\",\\\"Ivo reported at tick 71 that he personally ate berries and roots safely and also saw empty nearby food plants.\\\"],\\\"uncertainty\\\":\\\"Local replenishment timing and feasible cultivation methods remain unk